; The construction layer (P8): build_providers / build_extractor /
; build_fetch_stack / build_app, kept out of the server's startup path so
; [--check] can diagnose a deployment without building the MCP server. It is its
; own library — [seekwright.factory], wrapped as [Seekwright_factory] — for the
; same reason [lib/providers/] is one: the adapters depend on [seekwright], so a
; factory inside that library could not name them without closing a cycle
; (plans/seekwright-ocaml-port.md, the P4 note).

(library
 (name seekwright_factory)
 (public_name seekwright.factory)
 ; The five construction modules are behind the facade: what a caller may name
 ; is [Factory] and [Registry]. [provider_set] stays public because [factory.mli]
 ; re-exports its two records with their field labels, and a private module named
 ; from a public signature leaves a dangling path (plans/seekwright-ocaml-port.md,
 ; §11). The seal keeps installed consumers and odoc away from these five; a
 ; stanza inside this workspace can still reach them through dune's alias module,
 ; so the check-path boundary is pinned by source in [test/test_caps_audit.ml].
 (private_modules app fetch_stack grants providers_build verdict)
 (libraries
  seekwright
  seekwright.providers
  seekwright.fetch
  mcp-caps
  eio
  uri
  yojson))
